---
interface Props {
  framework?: 'nestjs' | 'inversify' | 'injectionjs';
}

const { framework } = Astro.props;
const nativeNames = {
  nestjs: 'NestJS TestingModule',
  inversify: 'InversifyJS Container',
  injectionjs: 'ReflectiveInjector',
};
const nativeName = framework ? nativeNames[framework] : 'Framework container';
const id = `container-comparison-${crypto.randomUUID()}`;
---

<figure class="container-comparison">
  <div class="diagram-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Compare framework container and Suites construction paths">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 840 320" role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-title ${id}-desc`}>
      <title id={`${id}-title`}>Framework IoC container and Suites TestBed</title>
      <desc id={`${id}-desc`}>Two construction paths for the same UserService. The framework container uses registered providers and its own factories and resolution rules. Its test configuration can register real dependencies or mocks. Suites reads injection metadata, creates dependency mocks, and constructs UserService. Sociable tests can expose selected real classes. Suites does not load the framework's provider registrations. Both approaches can use mocks.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id={`${id}-arrow`} viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10Z" class="arrowhead" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <rect class="panel" x="1" y="1" width="838" height="150" rx="10" />
      <text class="heading" x="20" y="28">Framework IoC container</text>
      <g class="edges" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}>
        <path d="M208 87H252" />
        <path d="M466 87H514" />
        <path d="M646 87H662V66H680" />
        <path d="M662 87V110H680" />
      </g>
      <rect class="node input" x="20" y="55" width="188" height="64" rx="7" />
      <text x="114" y="80" text-anchor="middle">Registrations</text>
      <text class="detail" x="114" y="102" text-anchor="middle">Modules / bindings / providers</text>
      <rect class="node engine" x="256" y="55" width="210" height="64" rx="7" />
      <text x="361" y="80" text-anchor="middle">{nativeName}</text>
      <text class="detail" x="361" y="102" text-anchor="middle">Factories + resolution rules</text>
      <rect class="node unit" x="518" y="55" width="128" height="64" rx="7" />
      <text class="code" x="582" y="80" text-anchor="middle">UserService</text>
      <text class="detail" x="582" y="102" text-anchor="middle">real class</text>
      <rect class="node real" x="684" y="49" width="136" height="34" rx="6" />
      <text x="752" y="71" text-anchor="middle">Real dependency</text>
      <rect class="node mock" x="684" y="93" width="136" height="34" rx="6" />
      <text x="752" y="115" text-anchor="middle">Mock provider</text>
      <text class="detail" x="20" y="140">Exercises the registrations included in this test.</text>

      <rect class="panel" x="1" y="165" width="838" height="154" rx="10" />
      <text class="heading" x="20" y="192">Suites TestBed</text>
      <g class="edges" marker-end={`url(#${id}-arrow)`}>
        <path d="M208 251H252" />
        <path d="M466 251H514" />
        <path d="M646 251H662V230H680" />
        <path d="M662 251V274H680" />
      </g>
      <rect class="node input" x="20" y="219" width="188" height="64" rx="7" />
      <text x="114" y="244" text-anchor="middle">Injection metadata</text>
      <text class="detail" x="114" y="266" text-anchor="middle">Constructor types + tokens</text>
      <rect class="node engine" x="256" y="219" width="210" height="64" rx="7" />
      <text x="361" y="244" text-anchor="middle">Suites TestBed</text>
      <text class="detail" x="361" y="266" text-anchor="middle">Generate mocks + construct</text>
      <rect class="node unit" x="518" y="219" width="128" height="64" rx="7" />
      <text class="code" x="582" y="244" text-anchor="middle">UserService</text>
      <text class="detail" x="582" y="266" text-anchor="middle">real class</text>
      <rect class="node mock" x="684" y="213" width="136" height="34" rx="6" />
      <text x="752" y="235" text-anchor="middle">Auto mock</text>
      <rect class="node real" x="684" y="257" width="136" height="34" rx="6" />
      <text x="752" y="279" text-anchor="middle">Exposed class</text>
      <text class="detail" x="20" y="308">Mocks by default; selected real classes with sociable().expose().</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Both approaches can use mocks. Native containers resolve test registrations; Suites builds the class from injection metadata. Solid dependency boxes are real; dashed boxes are mocks.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .container-comparison { margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .diagram-scroll { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; border-radius: 10px; }
  .diagram-scroll:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--primary-light); outline-offset: 4px; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 720px; max-width: 840px; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--text); font-family: var(--font-interface, sans-serif); font-size: 14px; }
  .heading { fill: var(--primary-light); font-weight: var(--fw-semibold); }
  .detail { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .code { font-family: var(--font-code); font-size: 13px; }
  .panel { fill: var(--bg-subtle); stroke: var(--border); }
  .node { fill: var(--surface); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.25; }
  .engine { fill: var(--primary-soft); stroke: var(--primary-border); }
  .unit { fill: var(--surface-raised); stroke: var(--primary-light); stroke-opacity: 0.65; stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .mock { stroke: var(--primary-light); stroke-opacity: 0.65; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .edges { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.25; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .arrowhead { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  figcaption { margin-top: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
